  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">APublica - Training of indigenous journalism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen the indigenous presence in the public debate by training indigenous communicators in investigative journalism on topics involving indigenous populations and their territories, mostly related to humand and environmental rights. The main objective is the training of indigenous communicators. There is a specific component of gender. The project intends that at least 50% of the communicators to be trained are indigenous women. Also, gender issues can be a subject of the news&apos; pieces to be developed.</narrative>
  </description>
